WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:24.960
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.390
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:34.570
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:41.210
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:47.930
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:54.670
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.670 --> 00:01:01.310
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:07.560
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:16.110
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.430
Our world’s gonna be
in the hands of pirates?!

12
00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:38.890
Wait a minute...
What are you telling us, Vegapunk?!

13
00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.520
No! Will our country
sink into the sea, too?!

14
00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.980
Do something, Marines!

15
00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:48.020
The world’s greatest genius confirmed it!

16
00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:49.480
Let’s go get it!

17
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:51.690
The One Piece is real!

18
00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.780
Pirates are going to rule the world!

19
00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:01.960
That’s what the world
sank into the sea for, right?!

20
00:02:01.960 --> 00:02:05.420
Brace yourselves, World Government!

21
00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:07.790
Why are we allowing this broadcast?!

22
00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:10.380
Transponder Snails around the prison
are broadcasting it!

23
00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:12.630
We don’t have a way to stop them!

24
00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:15.510
How could he say that?!

25
00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.600
Vegapunk!

26
00:02:23.980 --> 00:02:25.190
Luffy...

27
00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:27.480
I...

28
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.190
I’m...

29
00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:32.190
gonna be King of the Pirates!

30
00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:33.150
Whaaa?!

31
00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:37.120
Th-Th-The King of the Pirates is the person...

32
00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:40.830
who obtains everything this world has to offer!

33
00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.290
That means...

34
00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.710
you’re talking about
seeking the One Piece!

35
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.550
I...

36
00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:57.340
have to stop you
from achieving your dream!

37
00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.100
Buggy! Buggy!

38
00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:05.600
Buggy! Buggy! Buggy!

39
00:03:06.060 --> 00:03:08.060
Chairman Buggy!

40
00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:09.730
Show us...

41
00:03:10.110 --> 00:03:13.860
the world you’re going to create!

42
00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.860
Buggy! Buggy!

43
00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:18.870
Buggy...

44
00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.780
My world, you say?

45
00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:24.750
You absolute idiots...

46
00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.960
That ain’t what I’m after!

47
00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:32.630
What? Chairman Buggy...

48
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.600
It’s our world... Right?

49
00:03:46.930 --> 00:03:48.940
Buggy! Buggy!

50
00:03:48.940 --> 00:03:51.190
Chairman Buggy!

51
00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:54.820
We’ll follow you,
even to the depths of hell!

52
00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.940
Buggy! Buggy!

53
00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:00.660
Buggy! Buggy! Buggy!

54
00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:05.540
Sit.

55
00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:08.750
Yes, sir...

56
00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:12.960
Caribou?

57
00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.670
What do you want us to do, Teach?

58
00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:18.010
We’re fine with killing him, if you want...

59
00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:19.970
W-Wait a minute!

60
00:04:19.970 --> 00:04:23.510
The information I’ve got is sure to please ya,

61
00:04:23.510 --> 00:04:25.970
Master Teach!

62
00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:27.980
Bring him to me.

63
00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:28.730
Yes, sir!

64
00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:31.690
And if what he has to say
doesn’t blow me away...

65
00:04:31.690 --> 00:04:33.400
we blow him away.

66
00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.860
That’s the truth.

67
00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.910
Joyboy is...

68
00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:46.330
his...

69
00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:26.310
<b>The Void Fortnight</b>

70
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.010
Iron giant!

71
00:06:09.990 --> 00:06:12.830
It’s that horse-gramps again!

72
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.330
Nooo! Do something, Zoro!

73
00:06:37.310 --> 00:06:40.570
I’m sorry, Joyboy...

74
00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.950
You okay?! Giant Robo!

75
00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.870
I wanted to apologize!

76
00:06:54.330 --> 00:06:56.080
Deep down, I knew...

77
00:06:56.580 --> 00:06:59.750
that you couldn’t still be alive...

78
00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.210
Are you mixing me up with someone else?

79
00:07:05.880 --> 00:07:07.180
But...

80
00:07:08.010 --> 00:07:10.470
You look so much like him...

81
00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:13.430
It brings back...

82
00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:15.890
what I felt that day.

83
00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.490
An earthworm monster!

84
00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:35.830
We can’t escape! The ship’s gonna sink!

85
00:07:41.250 --> 00:07:42.590
I’m sorry...

86
00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:45.170
Joyboy...

87
00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:50.510
That I couldn’t make you king...

88
00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.220
“King”?

89
00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:55.680
You...

90
00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:57.980
What’s your name?

91
00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.230
I’m...

92
00:08:03.230 --> 00:08:06.190
Monkey D. Luffy!

93
00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:10.360
The man who’ll become the King of the Pirates!

94
00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:13.950
“D”...

95
00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:43.900
Hey, Luffy...

96
00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:09.880
Conqueror's haki?

97
00:09:12.970 --> 00:09:14.550
Thank you...

98
00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:18.640
for letting me hear the old rhythm...

99
00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:20.640
that I miss so much.

100
00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:28.150
Don’t die, okay?

101
00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:30.190
I won’t...

102
00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:33.660
let you die!

103
00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.000
Haki?!

104
00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.170
And it’s ridiculously strong...!

105
00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:53.050
Whose is it?!

106
00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.650
Great Imu!

107
00:10:52.070 --> 00:10:53.860
Joyboy!

108
00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.630
Guys!

109
00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.590
You’re all right!

110
00:11:12.550 --> 00:11:14.590
Luffy!

111
00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:21.050
I’m so glad we made it down safe!

112
00:11:21.930 --> 00:11:24.520
You’re the best, Jinbe!

113
00:11:27.690 --> 00:11:30.190
Made it by the skin of our teeth!

114
00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:31.820
We’re alive!

115
00:11:31.820 --> 00:11:35.440
Thought I was gonna die!

116
00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:39.780
I’m still not sure I believe we’re safe...

117
00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:44.540
Luffy! What happened
to those monsters?!

118
00:11:45.620 --> 00:11:48.040
Uhh, dunno...

119
00:11:50.420 --> 00:11:51.590
They disappeared...

120
00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:00.800
What’s goin’ on?

121
00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:02.760
A robot used haki?!

122
00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:05.270
How can haki make people disappear?!

123
00:12:08.560 --> 00:12:09.850
Nami!

124
00:12:10.230 --> 00:12:11.480
Are you okay?!

125
00:12:12.690 --> 00:12:14.860
We’re fine!

126
00:12:17.490 --> 00:12:20.860
But Atlas and Edison...

127
00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:03.660
Listen, Emet...

128
00:13:07.290 --> 00:13:09.160
Only when the time is right.

129
00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:11.620
Time is right?

130
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.840
I tied a knot of my greatest Haki...

131
00:13:14.840 --> 00:13:17.340
and sealed it inside of you!

132
00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:24.220
You’re going to keep on living
long after I’m gone.

133
00:13:24.640 --> 00:13:27.850
The day’ll come
when I can no longer help you.

134
00:13:27.850 --> 00:13:30.930
What? No way...

135
00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:34.980
When your life’s in danger...

136
00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.900
When someone you want to
protect is in danger...

137
00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:40.490
That’s when the time is right!

138
00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:42.650
Untie the knot then!

139
00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.870
When the time is right...

140
00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:48.240
you’ll save me...

141
00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:49.330
That’s right!

142
00:13:49.740 --> 00:13:52.660
I’ll reach out and help you
from the past!

143
00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:54.460
Just like I always do!

144
00:13:56.590 --> 00:13:58.800
I’m glad!

145
00:13:58.800 --> 00:14:00.760
Thank you!

146
00:14:00.760 --> 00:14:06.300
Then even after your death,
its like you’re still here with me!

147
00:14:06.300 --> 00:14:10.020
Hey, now! This is far
into the future now, got that?

148
00:14:11.730 --> 00:14:14.770
I’ll never, ever...

149
00:14:14.770 --> 00:14:16.980
ever...

150
00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:19.190
be lonely!

151
00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:32.950
Egghead! Come in!

152
00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:34.410
What the hell’s going on?!

153
00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.680
Captains!

154
00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.600
Hey! Find out what happened to ‘em!

155
00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:00.440
Aye-aye, Captain!

156
00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:05.700
Amazin’!

157
00:15:05.700 --> 00:15:08.070
That was conqueror’s haki, right?!

158
00:15:08.070 --> 00:15:11.240
Ya knocked out both
the monsters and the Marines!

159
00:15:11.240 --> 00:15:13.580
You're pretty cool, Robo!

160
00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:21.540
Captains!

161
00:15:21.960 --> 00:15:24.670
All of ‘em really are out cold!

162
00:15:24.670 --> 00:15:26.840
Are they? I can’t believe it!

163
00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:31.680
I couldn’t sense any hostility!
Could it be better than what Red Hair can do?

164
00:15:35.270 --> 00:15:38.600
How long are you all going to
keep sleeping?! Get up!

165
00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.230
You will take Us away from here!

166
00:15:42.650 --> 00:15:44.190
Wake up, you imbeciles!

167
00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:46.150
The Straw Hats are escaping!

168
00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.990
We owe ya one for savin’ us!

169
00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:56.910
Thanks a lot,

170
00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:59.540
Giant Robo!

171
00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:06.340
See ya later!

172
00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:12.760
All right! While they’re napping...

173
00:16:12.760 --> 00:16:14.430
let’s make ourselves scarce!

174
00:16:15.180 --> 00:16:16.390
You got it,

175
00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.810
Captains!

176
00:16:20.770 --> 00:16:24.820
Let’s get goin’, boys!

177
00:16:26.230 --> 00:16:29.110
To Elbaph!

178
00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:31.990
Set sail!

179
00:16:34.120 --> 00:16:36.790
We’re goin’ to Elbaph!

180
00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:39.660
Welcome back, Luffy!

181
00:16:46.550 --> 00:16:47.880
Luffy!

182
00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:51.090
I’m pooped...

183
00:16:51.090 --> 00:16:52.640
Huh?! You look terrible!

184
00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:55.310
Hey, Straw Hat! You okay?!

185
00:16:55.310 --> 00:16:56.890
We still got Hákarl if ya want!

186
00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:01.560
Masters!

187
00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:04.310
Thank you so much for coming!

188
00:17:04.310 --> 00:17:06.610
I missed you guys!

189
00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:10.150
Thank you all!

190
00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:15.490
Follow us, folks!
Don’t be slowpokes about it, now!

191
00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:18.620
Oh, yeah! I finally get to go to Elbaph!

192
00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:20.580
Jinbe!

193
00:17:20.580 --> 00:17:23.830
Aye! Full speed ahead it is!

194
00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:41.100
Let's get the dance floors
of the world bouncing, folks!

195
00:17:41.980 --> 00:17:44.980
We've got a fresh setlist of tracks!

196
00:17:46.020 --> 00:17:47.820
Incite fear!

197
00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.360
Paint the worst possible future!

198
00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:52.360
Make ‘em hang on our every word!

199
00:17:52.360 --> 00:17:55.740
All they can do is wait for the next WEJ!

200
00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.120
Actual scum.

201
00:17:59.790 --> 00:18:02.790
Vegapunk was offering us hope as well!

202
00:18:03.160 --> 00:18:05.960
Stay off my stage, kiddo!

203
00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:08.880
Or I’ll expose your whereabouts!

204
00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:14.090
Oh, have I offended you,
Mr. Big-Lie-Spreading Birdbrain?

205
00:18:14.880 --> 00:18:18.390
The wise won’t dance
to the tune of your lies!

206
00:18:19.760 --> 00:18:20.970
First of all, you...

207
00:18:20.970 --> 00:18:24.480
Now, now, dear Vivi...
Why don’t we calm down...

208
00:18:24.480 --> 00:18:28.360
Make him angry, and he’s gonna
put us out on the streets!

209
00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:33.070
You’re right. The truth can be
interesting, sometimes...

210
00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:36.410
So what if the world sinks into the sea?

211
00:18:36.860 --> 00:18:39.370
The sky’s my home!

212
00:18:39.370 --> 00:18:42.620
In that sense, it’s the dawning of my era!

213
00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.000
Say, Your Royal Highness...

214
00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:49.250
Maybe you oughta rethink
how you’re treating me, eh?

215
00:18:49.250 --> 00:18:54.130
Like I care? If the world’s ending,
I’m not putting my survival above anyone else’s!

216
00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:57.260
Hey, Vivi, you’ve really gotta...

217
00:18:57.260 --> 00:19:00.180
Check this out! We’ve got another
mountain of shocking news!

218
00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:03.980
Emperor Blackbeard
versus Trafalgar Law!

219
00:19:03.980 --> 00:19:07.810
Emperor Red Hair
versus Eustass “Captain” Kid!

220
00:19:07.810 --> 00:19:11.650
Emperor Straw Hat Luffy
kills Vegapunk!

221
00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.030
You’re a liar!

222
00:19:40.180 --> 00:19:41.720
Come in!

223
00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.060
What the hell’s going on?!

224
00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:49.440
I want to know
 what the hell that broadcast was!

225
00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:51.730
I want a sitrep yesterday!

226
00:19:51.730 --> 00:19:53.110
Come in, dammit!

227
00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:56.570
Are they all dead?

228
00:19:56.570 --> 00:19:58.910
What the hell happened, Egghead?!

229
00:19:59.320 --> 00:20:01.070
You’re quite loud, you know.

230
00:20:01.070 --> 00:20:03.870
Why are you the one answering?

231
00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:07.210
Borsalino! What happened to
the other sailors?!

232
00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:10.960
Every single one of them is sleeping.

233
00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:13.340
I don’t see them waking up for a while.

234
00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:15.090
Then what the hell is going on?!

235
00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:17.420
St. Saturn had better be safe!

236
00:20:17.420 --> 00:20:18.670
What about the Power Plant?!

237
00:20:18.670 --> 00:20:20.640
And the fugitives?!

238
00:20:24.390 --> 00:20:27.640
I’ll have a report sent in
once the young’uns wake up.

239
00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:31.100
You’d best not have half-assed your job,

240
00:20:31.100 --> 00:20:33.110
Borsalino!

241
00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:41.030
Let me ask you, Sakazuki...
Have you ever...

242
00:20:43.070 --> 00:20:46.540
killed a close friend of yours?

243
00:20:55.590 --> 00:20:57.710
Your head is huge!

244
00:20:57.710 --> 00:21:02.680
Nice to meet you.
I’m Borsalino, a Marine.

245
00:21:07.640 --> 00:21:09.100
How much can you provide?

246
00:21:09.100 --> 00:21:10.020
Hmm?

247
00:21:10.020 --> 00:21:12.020
My arrest is just an excuse.

248
00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:14.610
You people just want my brain.

249
00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:17.820
How much can you pay
in research funds?

250
00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:22.030
You’re an interesting man!

251
00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:27.030
So this is your plan for the island?

252
00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:29.790
I’m going to call it Egghead!

253
00:21:29.790 --> 00:21:32.210
We're building the future 500 years ahead!

254
00:21:32.210 --> 00:21:34.290
Will you give me a hand, Borsalino?

255
00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:38.880
I can’t, I’m an Admiral now.

256
00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:42.130
Don’t drop it, Uncle!
You ain’t standin’ straight!

257
00:21:42.130 --> 00:21:44.720
I’m counting on you, Borsalino!

258
00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:04.780
This island, Egghead,

259
00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:09.620
is packed to the brim with the fruits of
cutting-edge research from every field of study!

260
00:22:10.080 --> 00:22:14.580
Destroy it, and you’ll set
scientific progress back a hundred years!

261
00:22:14.580 --> 00:22:16.790
Rescind the Buster Call!

262
00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:20.420
Please, Kizaru!

263
00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:37.270
You accuse me of having
“half-assed” my job, Sakazuki...

264
00:22:37.730 --> 00:22:40.270
If you have the time to
sit on your ass and doubt me,

265
00:22:40.270 --> 00:22:43.860
then come take a look with your own
damn eyes, you ungrateful brat!

266
00:22:52.700 --> 00:22:55.250
I’m sorry, brother...

267
00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:57.210
Don’t even start...

268
00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:15.560
I don’t really get it, Vegapunk...

269
00:23:16.890 --> 00:23:19.400
What you said at that moment, I mean.

270
00:23:21.860 --> 00:23:23.860
Is this the result you were shooting for?

271
00:23:25.150 --> 00:23:27.950
C’mon. I couldn’t ask you
what you really meant,

272
00:23:27.950 --> 00:23:29.950
but you said some pretty outrageous stuff.

273
00:23:29.950 --> 00:23:32.450
We’re heading down to save Bonney,

274
00:23:32.910 --> 00:23:35.450
and I’m going to stay down there!

275
00:23:35.450 --> 00:23:37.410
Huh?! But you’d die!

276
00:23:37.410 --> 00:23:38.460
Don’t try to save me.

277
00:23:38.920 --> 00:23:41.250
Just let me die then and there!

278
00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:56.000
Egghead

Two weeks before
the Straw Hats' Arrival

279
00:23:55.680 --> 00:23:56.480
What on...?

280
00:24:02.310 --> 00:24:03.360
This is...!

281
00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:04.820
Stella! Pythagoras!

282
00:24:05.530 --> 00:24:08.400
There are irregularities in the readings
from the Power Plant?!

283
00:24:08.400 --> 00:24:10.030
There is no mistaking it...

284
00:24:10.030 --> 00:24:13.700
Look at the changes in the
particle number density and the neutron flux.

285
00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:18.160
The energy expenditure on the Seraphim
has been slowly incremented over time.

286
00:24:18.160 --> 00:24:20.710
If this is a mistake in our calculations,
it is a grave one.

287
00:24:20.710 --> 00:24:25.840
Oh, oh? These values
don’t match the ones we verified!

288
00:24:25.840 --> 00:24:27.760
The reaction rate is rising...

289
00:24:27.760 --> 00:24:30.050
yet the Power Plant remains stable!

290
00:24:30.050 --> 00:24:31.390
Indeed.

291
00:24:31.390 --> 00:24:36.390
Which means this data is evidence that
someone stole a portion of the Mother Flame.

292
00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:41.850
All the readings with respect to the Power Plant
were carefully manipulated.

293
00:24:42.810 --> 00:24:45.020
The only person capable of this...

294
00:24:45.020 --> 00:24:46.530
is a Vegapunk!

295
00:24:47.070 --> 00:24:48.690
Is it Lilith?!

296
00:24:48.690 --> 00:24:51.280
Now, now, we don’t have
confirmation yet!

297
00:24:51.280 --> 00:24:56.490
Unfortunately,
only we three have airtight alibis.

298
00:24:56.490 --> 00:24:58.910
A vast quantity of energy was stolen.

299
00:24:58.910 --> 00:25:01.710
So you’re saying it’s one of
the remaining four, yes?

300
00:25:01.710 --> 00:25:03.080
Most likely Lilith!

301
00:25:03.080 --> 00:25:06.000
That’s why you had us
put our brains into stealth mode!

302
00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:10.300
Yes, if this experience is shared
with Punk Records, Lili—

303
00:25:10.300 --> 00:25:12.260
the culprit will notice we’ve noticed.

304
00:25:12.260 --> 00:25:16.220
We will absolutely find out
who did this!

305
00:25:17.140 --> 00:25:17.970
Mm-hmm!

306
00:25:18.790 --> 00:25:22.540
Egghead

A week before
the Straw Hats' arrival

307
00:25:22.560 --> 00:25:25.020
Damn! Not a single lead!

308
00:25:25.020 --> 00:25:26.570
Lilith is clean!

309
00:25:26.570 --> 00:25:28.570
All four of them have alibis.

310
00:25:28.570 --> 00:25:29.860
Why can’t we find anything?!

311
00:25:29.860 --> 00:25:32.780
Oh dear! Oh dear! I've identified the culprit!

312
00:25:32.780 --> 00:25:33.990
It’s York!

313
00:25:33.990 --> 00:25:37.830
What?! York?!

314
00:25:37.830 --> 00:25:41.830
The information she synchronized
with Punk Records were dummy memories!

315
00:25:41.830 --> 00:25:46.750
Videos from the Camsnails
on the route she took were also fabricated!

316
00:25:47.420 --> 00:25:49.130
Gimme seconds...

317
00:25:49.590 --> 00:25:51.170
But for what purpose?!

318
00:25:52.300 --> 00:25:54.090
And sorry, Lilith!

319
00:25:55.680 --> 00:25:58.350
There are signs of the Sea Beast Weapons
being manipulated.

320
00:25:58.350 --> 00:26:02.310
Found evidence of use of the White
Transponder Snail to block eavesdropping!

321
00:26:02.310 --> 00:26:03.060
Found it!

322
00:26:03.640 --> 00:26:07.690
Successfully recovered the data
from the Long-Distance Transponder Snail!

323
00:26:12.860 --> 00:26:16.990
Dr. Vegapunk is researching
the Void Century.

324
00:26:16.990 --> 00:26:17.700
What?!

325
00:26:17.700 --> 00:26:20.080
Is this a transmission to Mary Geoise?!

326
00:26:20.080 --> 00:26:23.750
This explains why Cipher Pol
kept coming back to investigate!

327
00:26:28.190 --> 00:26:40.870
Six days before
the Straw Hats' Arrival

328
00:26:29.460 --> 00:26:31.840
I heard the Kingdom of Lulusia vanished!

329
00:26:31.840 --> 00:26:36.340
We don’t have full details yet,
but I do have this sense of dread!

330
00:26:36.340 --> 00:26:40.060
Pythagoras! Keep a close eye
on the radio signals and the groundwater level!

331
00:26:40.060 --> 00:26:40.890
I will!

332
00:26:40.890 --> 00:26:43.680
Does this have something to do
with the stolen Mother Flame?

333
00:26:43.680 --> 00:26:44.940
It does!

334
00:26:44.940 --> 00:26:50.360
She must have transported the Mother Flame via
the Sea Beast Weapons and handed it to the Government.

335
00:26:50.360 --> 00:26:52.570
If I may speculate,

336
00:26:52.570 --> 00:26:55.990
I’d say the Government
possesses the Ancient Weapons!

337
00:26:55.990 --> 00:26:59.830
And they were most likely activated
using the Mother Flame that York gave them.

338
00:26:59.830 --> 00:27:01.370
We’ll soon see the results.

339
00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:04.330
This is the most likely scenario...

340
00:27:04.330 --> 00:27:06.790
Yet I can’t go public with it.

341
00:27:07.210 --> 00:27:08.830
This is all my fault!

342
00:27:08.830 --> 00:27:10.250
Stella...

343
00:27:10.250 --> 00:27:14.010
I should never have isolated greed
from the human mind!

344
00:27:16.720 --> 00:27:20.970
If we apprehend her,
is there anything else we can do?

345
00:27:20.970 --> 00:27:22.970
No, we’re far too late.

346
00:27:22.970 --> 00:27:24.980
Regardless of her objective,

347
00:27:24.980 --> 00:27:28.100
those who study the Void Century
are erased from existence!

348
00:27:28.100 --> 00:27:33.190
She proved her worth to them by
carelessly handing over the Mother Flame.

349
00:27:33.190 --> 00:27:38.160
If it had been us, we would’ve thoroughly
examined their objectives and all aspects of safety!

350
00:27:38.740 --> 00:27:42.120
Stella, we can still escape...

351
00:27:42.120 --> 00:27:44.790
Then I re-quasar you ready a ship!

352
00:27:44.790 --> 00:27:48.080
This is to allow the residents
of Egghead to escape!

353
00:27:48.790 --> 00:27:51.080
But for us, we cannot escape.

354
00:27:51.080 --> 00:27:54.800
Secret orders will have already been
issued to all naval branches.

355
00:27:56.760 --> 00:27:59.800
We’d be chased to the ends of the world.

356
00:27:59.800 --> 00:28:03.760
If we die on the run,
our deaths would be in vain.

357
00:28:03.760 --> 00:28:10.770
But Egghead has resources
that Ohara didn’t, 22 years ago!

358
00:28:10.770 --> 00:28:13.730
It has the means to
maximize the reach of my voice!

359
00:28:15.610 --> 00:28:19.700
Anyway... the closer I get to it,
the darker and more obscure it becomes!

360
00:28:20.280 --> 00:28:23.700
What is the World Government, truly?!

361
00:28:25.450 --> 00:28:28.410
I will die, but it won’t be in vain!

362
00:28:29.620 --> 00:28:32.670
I’m sorry for involving you two.

363
00:28:33.210 --> 00:28:35.880
Don’t be. We’re Vegapunks, too.

364
00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:38.470
We were thinking the same thing!

365
00:28:41.800 --> 00:28:45.890
But, Stella, remember...
Our definition of “death” is unique.

366
00:28:45.890 --> 00:28:49.980
Indeed. There is one other thing
that we must protect...

367
00:28:49.980 --> 00:28:52.600
The Cloud Plant,
the island clouds generator!

368
00:28:52.600 --> 00:28:56.320
Island clouds could play a vital role
in saving mankind in the future.

369
00:29:02.240 --> 00:29:02.990
Whuh?

370
00:29:03.660 --> 00:29:06.450
Stella! Whatcha doin’ here?

371
00:29:06.450 --> 00:29:09.120
Oh, it’s you, York...

372
00:29:09.120 --> 00:29:11.000
The same thing I’m always doing!

373
00:29:11.000 --> 00:29:13.420
An operational experiment
using the Mother Flame!

374
00:29:13.420 --> 00:29:18.000
If we could run this thing with it,
it would be the ideal energy source!

375
00:29:18.710 --> 00:29:21.970
You’re right! I hope ya finish
your experiment soon!

376
00:29:22.340 --> 00:29:23.470
Yup!

377
00:29:24.390 --> 00:29:27.390
Its incomplete state is our only hope.

378
00:29:27.370 --> 00:29:33.630
Two days before
the Straw Hats' Arrival

379
00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:31.390
Go ahead and talk.
I’ve started recording.

380
00:29:32.390 --> 00:29:35.310
Um... Hello?

381
00:29:35.310 --> 00:29:36.570
Check, check...

382
00:29:36.570 --> 00:29:39.860
Hello, world! Come in, world!

383
00:29:41.650 --> 00:29:43.820
I am Dr. Vegapunk!

384
00:29:44.200 --> 00:29:46.830
A humble genius scientist!

385
00:29:50.580 --> 00:29:52.500
It will come as a shock, I’m sure...

386
00:29:52.500 --> 00:29:56.250
But it is the truth,
and all have the right to know!

387
00:29:57.170 --> 00:30:01.340
No one will expect that
the Transponder Snail is hidden in here!

388
00:30:01.340 --> 00:30:04.970
My death will be
the trigger for the broadcast.

389
00:30:06.010 --> 00:30:11.220
And to ensure she doesn’t discover
what we set up, even by the remotest chance,

390
00:30:11.220 --> 00:30:14.270
we’ll wipe it from our memories.

391
00:30:14.270 --> 00:30:18.730
But in exchange,
other memories will also be lost.

392
00:30:19.900 --> 00:30:24.030
We’ll have to find out again that
York stole the Mother Flame and sold us out.

393
00:30:24.030 --> 00:30:27.280
We’ll also realize
that we’re being targeted,

394
00:30:27.780 --> 00:30:30.200
and we will be startled anew.

395
00:30:30.200 --> 00:30:31.120
Very much so.

396
00:30:31.870 --> 00:30:34.500
We’ll experience the terror
as if for the first time.

397
00:30:34.500 --> 00:30:36.670
But, we have already taken measures!

398
00:30:38.210 --> 00:30:41.460
And the utter disaster that awaits
just around the corner...

399
00:30:41.460 --> 00:30:43.510
is none other than
our ultimate triumph!

400
00:30:54.930 --> 00:30:56.770
Shaka, what were we doing?

401
00:30:56.770 --> 00:30:57.690
I don’t know.

402
00:30:58.310 --> 00:30:59.690
Why are we here?

403
00:30:59.690 --> 00:31:02.230
This is our memory mass testing lab...

404
00:31:02.230 --> 00:31:05.150
Perhaps we were conducting a test?

405
00:31:07.610 --> 00:31:09.870
This is my handwriting...

406
00:31:10.410 --> 00:31:11.950
“Good morning, everyone."

407
00:31:11.950 --> 00:31:16.210
"There is now a Void Fortnight
in your memories,"

408
00:31:16.210 --> 00:31:19.290
"but this was by your own choice."

409
00:31:19.290 --> 00:31:21.920
"There are more surprises in store for you,"

410
00:31:21.920 --> 00:31:23.050
"LOL.”

411
00:31:23.050 --> 00:31:24.460
Wha?!

412
00:31:24.460 --> 00:31:26.970
“I’ll share just this with you:"

413
00:31:26.970 --> 00:31:30.600
"The World Government discovered
our research into the Void Century,"

414
00:31:30.600 --> 00:31:33.810
"but I’ve taken
the best possible measures."

415
00:31:34.520 --> 00:31:36.640
"Just trust yourself,"

416
00:31:36.640 --> 00:31:37.810
"and die.”

417
00:31:38.190 --> 00:31:41.110
What?! They found out?!

418
00:31:41.110 --> 00:31:43.110
And you’re telling us to “die”?!
No chance!

419
00:31:43.110 --> 00:31:44.900
“And one more thing..."

420
00:31:47.650 --> 00:31:51.950
What is all this stuff?!

421
00:31:52.370 --> 00:31:56.160
Stella! Emperor Straw Hat’s crew
have arrived, along with Bonney!

422
00:31:56.160 --> 00:31:57.620
What?!

423
00:31:58.710 --> 00:32:00.460
CP-0 has landed!

424
00:32:00.460 --> 00:32:01.670
What?!

425
00:32:03.920 --> 00:32:06.380
We’re surrounded by Marine ships!

426
00:32:06.380 --> 00:32:07.840
What?!

427
00:32:08.340 --> 00:32:11.220
It’s Admiral Kizaru
and St. Saturn of the Five Elders!

428
00:32:11.220 --> 00:32:12.890
What?!

429
00:32:14.890 --> 00:32:17.350
We’re heading down to save Bonney,

430
00:32:17.930 --> 00:32:20.310
and I’m going to stay down there!

431
00:32:20.310 --> 00:32:21.810
Huh?! But you’d die!

432
00:32:21.810 --> 00:32:23.270
Don’t try to save me.

433
00:32:23.270 --> 00:32:25.530
Just let me die then and there!

434
00:32:25.530 --> 00:32:27.690
What?! You got a death wish
or something?!

435
00:32:27.690 --> 00:32:31.990
No, but I have this feeling my death
will bring about something significant!

436
00:32:31.990 --> 00:32:34.830
Don’t even joke about that!
I’m protectin’ ya!

437
00:32:34.830 --> 00:32:39.120
Yeah, it’ll cause huge-ass riots!
We can’t let you die!

438
00:32:39.540 --> 00:32:41.330
Pretty please?!

439
00:32:45.090 --> 00:32:48.210
To our reunion with old friends!

440
00:32:48.210 --> 00:32:50.760
Cheers!

441
00:32:52.090 --> 00:32:54.510
Onward to Elbaph!
Onward to my dream!

442
00:32:56.890 --> 00:32:58.980
And you know, about the One Piece...

443
00:33:00.180 --> 00:33:01.440
What are you...?!

444
00:33:01.850 --> 00:33:04.480
I want your crew
to be the ones to get it!

445
00:33:07.860 --> 00:33:11.700
No, wait... Not now, later...

